{
    "name":  "loom-sync-engine",
    "description":  "Tested, modular engine for Loom's Command Center sync (prompt v3.14). It handles everything mechanical: the schema as data, request params, page saving with count checks, Calendar identity and timing invariants, per-source scope rules, normalization, enrichment cap, upsert and guarded close batches, run lock, on-demand schema validation, verify, and the 7-line report. Loom only makes the tool calls and does enrichment.",
    "whenToUse":  "At the start of every Loom sync or rebuild run (scheduled or \"@Loom sync now\"). Fetch it with FetchSkillScripts and follow the runbook. Never rewrite sync, parsing or report code by hand.",
